## Experience and Lessons
|Case|:add_product_to_cart
```pseudocode
FUNCTION add_to_cart(username, product_id)
    cart_items = load_cart(username)
    IF product_id NOT IN cart_items
        APPEND product_id TO cart_items
        CALL save_cart(username, cart_items)
        RETURN True
    ENDIF
    RETURN False
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION load_cart(username)
    INITIALIZE cart_items AS empty list
    TRY
        OPEN cart_file IN read mode
            FOR EACH line IN cart_file
                SPLIT line INTO user, product_ids
                IF user == username
                    cart_items = SPLIT product_ids BY ','
                    RETURN cart_items
                ENDIF
            ENDFOR
        CLOSE cart_file
    EXCEPT FileNotFoundError
        RETURN empty list
    END TRY
    RETURN cart_items
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION save_cart(username, cart_items)
    OPEN cart_file IN write mode
        WRITE username, '|', JOIN cart_items BY ',' TO cart_file
    CLOSE cart_file
END FUNCTION
```
- Key Functionality: Adds a product to the user's cart if it is not already present.
- Special Libraries: None used.

4. |Case|:checkout_process
```pseudocode
FUNCTION create_order(username, product_ids, shipping_address, payment_info)
    OPEN orders_file IN append mode
        WRITE username, '|', JOIN product_ids BY ',', '|', shipping_address, '|', payment_info TO orders_file
    CLOSE orders_file
    RETURN True
END FUNCTION
```
- Key Functionality: Creates a new order by writing the order details to the orders file.
- Special Libraries: None used.

